WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.136
CUBE expands the idea further by producing every
grouping combination With

00:00:06.162 --> 00:00:11.952
category and product that includes
category-and-product detail category totals product
totals

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:17.556
across categories and the grand total Run the
example and compare

00:00:17.582 --> 00:00:22.384
the number and type of rows with the ROLLUP result
The key

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:26.397
difference is that ROLLUP follows a hierarchy while
CUBE creates totals for

00:00:26.423 --> 00:00:32.077
every dimension combination CUBE can be useful for
exploratory summary

00:00:32.103 --> 00:00:35.708
tables but the number of combinations grows quickly
when you add more

00:00:35.722 --> 00:00:41.457
dimensions Before using CUBE in a larger dataset
think about how many

00:00:41.471 --> 00:00:45.221
grouping combinations you are requesting and whether
each one supports a real

00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:46.207
analytical need
